As soon as PvP was introduced in SotA Release 8, Duke Violation and the Order of Vengeance Guild hosted the very first PvP tournament in Shroud of the Avatar on July 24, 2014. Here's a screeenshot and excerpt about those first tournaments from Update of the Avatar #84:

The Order of Vengeance Guild hosted multiple tournaments starting on Thursday, July 24th and continuing through the weekend. The tournaments were held on The Brave Coast player island. Vengeance members procured two boats, a light house, and a Knight's Keep across the pond from Lord British's castle. The fights occurred on the beach with spectators watching from the bow of the boat.

//d2sx9mrt4zumaq.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/SotA_R8_pic13.jpg

The Order of Vengeance (along with other PvP-friendly groups such as The Bear Tavern, BMC, etc.), have been instrumental in helping us evolve combat and PvP in SotA. Thus, when we introduced the ability for Player Owned Towns to be flagged as Open PvP in Release 18, we chose Vengeance as the first PoT to test that functionality. Additionally, it allowed us to test the Desert biome template that Abe Robertson adapted from Michael Hutchison's original PaxLair forest biome template.

//d2sx9mrt4zumaq.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/SotA_PoT_Template_Desert_1.jpg

